-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 4 (b): ss 45 to 53, retrenchment and
-- retirement benefit, the priority of gratuities, annual wage supplements, wage
-- recommendations, the power to suspend this Part, and the offence.
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore
-- Statutes Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every
-- `-- src:` line copies a line of that file (script-generated); every quotation in
-- a FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment is a phrase of it (checked by a script).
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its
-- own words.  NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts and is never to
-- be read as no.  "marginal (a)" or "marginal (b)" marks the branches that rest on
-- one of the two readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 4 Rest days, hours of work and other conditions of service, ss 45 to 53`

§§ `s 45 Payment of retrenchment benefit`

-- Two years of continuous service are complete on the second anniversary of the day service began;
-- before that day the service is "less than 2 years".
-- src:2099 | 45. No employee who has been in continuous service with an
-- src:2100 | employer for less than 2 years is entitled to any retrenchment benefit
-- src:2101 | on his or her dismissal on the ground of redundancy or by reason of
-- src:2102 | any reorganisation of the employer’s profession, business, trade or
-- src:2103 | work.
@ref s 45 (src:2099-2103)
GIVEN `the day the employee's continuous service with the employer began` IS A DATE
      `the day of dismissal` IS A DATE
      `the employee is dismissed on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45 the employee is entitled to a retrenchment benefit on dismissal` MEANS
    IF `the employee is dismissed on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work` AND (`the day of dismissal` LESS THAN `the second anniversary`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No employee who has been in continuous service with an employer for less than 2 years is entitled to any retrenchment benefit on his or her dismissal on the ground of redundancy" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 45 says who is not entitled and does not say that anyone else is
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the second anniversary` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY `the day the employee's continuous service with the employer began`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the employee's continuous service with the employer began`) ((DATE_YEAR `the day the employee's continuous service with the employer began`) PLUS 2)

§§ `s 46 Retirement benefit`

-- src:2109 | 46. No employee who has been in continuous service with an
-- src:2110 | employer for less than 5 years is entitled to any retirement benefit
-- src:2111 | other than the sums payable under the Central Provident Fund
-- src:2112 | Act 1953 on the cessation of his or her service with the employer.
@ref s 46 (src:2109-2112)
GIVEN `the day the employee's continuous service with the employer began` IS A DATE
      `the day the employee's service with the employer ceased` IS A DATE
      `the benefit is a retirement benefit other than the sums payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 the employee is entitled to a retirement benefit on the cessation of service` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is a retirement benefit other than the sums payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` AND (`the day the employee's service with the employer ceased` LESS THAN `the fifth anniversary`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No employee who has been in continuous service with an employer for less than 5 years is entitled to any retirement benefit other than the sums payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 46 says who is not entitled and does not say that anyone else is
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the fifth anniversary` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY `the day the employee's continuous service with the employer began`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the employee's continuous service with the employer began`) ((DATE_YEAR `the day the employee's continuous service with the employer began`) PLUS 5)

§§ `s 47 Priority of retirement benefits, etc.`

DECLARE `s 47(1) Insolvency proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `s 47(1)(a) the winding up of a company under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 47(1)(b) the distribution of the property of a bankrupt or of a person dying insolvent under section 352 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 47(1)(c) the winding up of a VCC under the repealed section 328 of the Companies Act 1967 as applied before the operative date`
    `s 47(1)(d) the winding up of a VCC under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 as applied on the operative date`
    `s 47(1)(e) the winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC under the repealed section 328 of the Companies Act 1967 as applied before the operative date`
    `s 47(1)(f) the winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 as applied on the operative date`
    `s 47(1) some other proceeding`

-- The "operative date" is the date of commencement of ss 29, 48 and 62 of the Variable Capital
-- Companies (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2019, which is not among the sources (subsection (5)):
-- the caller picks the paragraph that fits the proceeding.
