@ref s 47(1) (src:2116-2183)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `s 47(1) Insolvency proceeding`
      `a collective agreement or an award contains a provision for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money to the employee on retirement or on the termination of services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gratuity or other sum of money is due and owing to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a collective agreement or an award contains a provision for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money to an employee ... the gratuity or other sum of money which is due and owing to the employee" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "Where" not met
        IF NOT (`a collective agreement or an award contains a provision for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money to the employee on retirement or on the termination of services` AND `the gratuity or other sum of money is due and owing to the employee`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs (a) to (f) are the only proceedings subsection (1) names
        IF proceeding EQUALS `s 47(1) some other proceeding` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 47(1) (src:2116-2183)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `s 47(1) Insolvency proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money ranks after the preferential debts` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (b) does not say where the gratuity ranks, and a proceeding outside paragraphs (a) to (f) is not spoken of
    WHEN `s 47(1)(b) the distribution of the property of a bankrupt or of a person dying insolvent under section 352 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `s 47(1) some other proceeding` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2187 | (2) Where a collective agreement or an award contains a provision
-- src:2188 | for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money to an employee
-- src:2189 | on his or her retirement and no provision is made for the payment of a
-- src:2190 | gratuity or other sum of money on the termination of the employee’s
-- src:2191 | services by reason of his or her employer ceasing to carry on business
-- src:2192 | for whatever reason, or by reason of the employer transferring the
-- src:2193 | whole or part of the employer’s undertaking or property (as the case
-- src:2194 | may be), every such collective agreement or award is deemed, despite
-- src:2195 | anything contained in any written law or rule of law or collective
-- src:2196 | agreement or award to the contrary, to contain a provision that in the
-- src:2197 | event of the employer ceasing to carry on business for whatever
-- src:2198 | reason or transferring the whole or part of the employer’s undertaking
-- src:2199 | or property (as the case may be), an employee who ceases to be
-- src:2200 | employed by the employer by reason of the happening of such a
-- src:2201 | contingency must be paid such sum of money as the employee would
-- src:2202 | have been entitled to receive under the terms of the collective
-- src:2203 | agreement or award if the employee had retired from the service of
-- src:2204 | the employer on the day the employer ceases to carry on business or
-- src:2205 | transfers the whole or part of the employer’s undertaking or property,
-- src:2206 | as the case may be.
@ref s 47(2) (src:2187-2206)
GIVEN `a collective agreement or an award contains a provision for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money to an employee on retirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no provision is made for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money on the termination of the employee's services by reason of the employer ceasing to carry on business or transferring the whole or part of the undertaking or property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has ceased to carry on business or has transferred the whole or part of the undertaking or property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has ceased to be employed by the employer by reason of that contingency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (3) takes subsection (2) away` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(2) the collective agreement or award is deemed to contain the provision that the employee must be paid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a collective agreement or an award contains a provision for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money to an employee on his or her retirement and no provision is made for" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "Where" not met
        IF NOT (`a collective agreement or an award contains a provision for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money to an employee on retirement` AND `no provision is made for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money on the termination of the employee's services by reason of the employer ceasing to carry on business or transferring the whole or part of the undertaking or property`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not apply where an employer has set up a fund under a scheme for the payment of pensions, gratuities, provident fund or other superannuation benefits" -- subsection (3)
        IF `subsection (3) takes subsection (2) away` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the employer has ceased to carry on business or has transferred the whole or part of the undertaking or property` AND `the employee has ceased to be employed by the employer by reason of that contingency` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the event of the employer ceasing to carry on business for whatever reason or transferring the whole or part of the employer’s undertaking or property" -- the contingency is the content of the deemed provision, not a condition of the deeming, so the function leaves the case before it happens unanswered
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 47(2) (src:2187-2206)
GIVEN `the sum of money the employee would have been entitled to receive under the terms of the collective agreement or award if the employee had retired from the service of the employer on the day the employer ceased to carry on business or transferred the undertaking or property` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of s 47(2) the provision is deemed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 47(2) the sum of money the employee must be paid` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 47(2) the provision is deemed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `the sum of money the employee would have been entitled to receive under the terms of the collective agreement or award if the employee had retired from the service of the employer on the day the employer ceased to carry on business or transferred the undertaking or property`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sum is payable only where subsection (2) deems the provision to be in the collective agreement or award
    ELSE NOTHING

