§§ `s 48 Payment of annual wage supplement or other variable payment`

-- The Act's date of 26 August 1988 is a date in the sentence ("made before 26 August 1988").
-- src:2266 | 48.—(1) Where a contract of service or collective agreement made
-- src:2267 | before 26 August 1988 provides for the payment by the employer of
-- src:2268 | any annual wage supplement, annual bonus or annual wage increase,
-- src:2269 | the payments continue to be payable by the employer until the
-- src:2274 | employer and the employer’s employees or a trade union representing
-- src:2275 | the employer’s employees have negotiated and agreed to vary the
-- src:2276 | payments.
@ref s 48(1) (src:2266-2276)
GIVEN `the day the contract of service or collective agreement was made` IS A DATE
      `it provides for the payment by the employer of an annual wage supplement, annual bonus or annual wage increase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer and the employer's employees or a trade union representing them have negotiated and agreed to vary the payments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) the payments continue to be payable by the employer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a contract of service or collective agreement made before 26 August 1988 provides for the payment by the employer of any annual wage supplement, annual bonus or annual wage increase" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a) and (b): a "Where" not met, and a day outside the period the text fixes
        IF NOT ((`the day the contract of service or collective agreement was made` LESS THAN Date 26 8 1988) AND `it provides for the payment by the employer of an annual wage supplement, annual bonus or annual wage increase`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the payments continue to be payable by the employer until" ... "have negotiated and agreed to vary the payments" -- marginal (a)
        IF `the employer and the employer's employees or a trade union representing them have negotiated and agreed to vary the payments` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

