@ref s 48(3) (src:2283-2289)
GIVEN `the employer paid an annual wage supplement before 26 August 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the contract of service or collective agreement was made` IS A DATE
      `the annual wage supplement the provision allows` IS A NUMBER
      `one month's wages of the employees` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(3) the contract of service or collective agreement may contain the provision for the annual wage supplement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an employer has not paid any annual wage supplement prior to 26 August 1988, any contract of service or collective agreement made on or after that date"
        IF `the employer paid an annual wage supplement before 26 August 1988` OR (`the day the contract of service or collective agreement was made` LESS THAN Date 26 8 1988) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not contain a provision for the payment of an annual wage supplement exceeding the equivalent of one month’s wages of the employees" -- marginal (a)
        IF `the annual wage supplement the provision allows` GREATER THAN `one month's wages of the employees` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) says what the contract or collective agreement must not contain and does not say that a provision within one month's wages is allowed
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The "Where" of subsection (3) as a yes/no question of its own (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)): the
-- cap of one month's wages binds a contract or collective agreement made on or after
-- 26 August 1988 of an employer that paid no annual wage supplement before that date.
-- The function above says what a contract within or above the cap may contain.
@ref s 48(3) (src:2283-2289)
GIVEN `the employer paid an annual wage supplement before 26 August 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the contract of service or collective agreement was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(3) the cap of one month's wages on the annual wage supplement applies` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the employer paid an annual wage supplement before 26 August 1988`) AND (NOT (`the day the contract of service or collective agreement was made` LESS THAN Date 26 8 1988))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an employer has not paid any annual wage supplement prior to 26 August 1988, any contract of service or collective agreement made on or after that date" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a) and (b): a "Where" not met, and a day outside the period the text fixes
    ELSE JUST FALSE
