      `the annual wage supplement paid` IS A NUMBER
      `one month's wages of the employees` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(4) the employer that pays an annual wage supplement above the amount in subsection (3) is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer pays an annual wage supplement` AND (`the annual wage supplement paid` GREATER THAN `one month's wages of the employees`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any employer who pays an annual wage supplement exceeding the amount specified in subsection (3)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (4) states no penalty.  The penalty "for which no penalty is otherwise provided" is
-- in section 112 (ea2), which the caller's answer carries (seam S15).
@ref s 48(4) (src:2291-2296)
GIVEN `the answer of s 112 first conviction` IS A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
      `the answer of s 112 subsequent conviction` IS A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
      `the person has been convicted of an offence before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
`s 48(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (4) states no penalty, and the penalty for which none is otherwise provided is in section 112
    IF `the person has been convicted of an offence before` THEN `the answer of s 112 subsequent conviction` ELSE `the answer of s 112 first conviction`

-- src:2298 | (5) Even though an annual wage supplement may be payable under
-- src:2299 | subsection (1) or (3), an employer may, in the event of exceptionally
-- src:2300 | poor business results for any year, invite the employees or a trade
-- src:2301 | union representing the employer’s employees to negotiate for a lower
-- src:2302 | quantum of annual wage supplement or for no annual wage
-- src:2303 | supplement to be paid for that year.
@ref s 48(5) (src:2298-2303)
GIVEN `the year's business results are exceptionally poor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(5) the employer may invite the employees or a trade union to negotiate for a lower annual wage supplement or none` MEANS
    IF `the year's business results are exceptionally poor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the event of exceptionally poor business results for any year" -- "in the event of" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled: fork F-EVENT); ruled 2026-11-05 (b)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 49 Power of Minister to make recommendations for wage adjustments`

-- src:2308 | 49. The Minister may make recommendations for wage adjustment,
-- src:2309 | and upon the publication of the recommendations in the Gazette the
-- src:2310 | employer and the employer’s employees or a trade union representing
-- src:2311 | the employer’s employees may negotiate based on those
-- src:2312 | recommendations.
@ref s 49 (src:2308-2312)
GIVEN `the person is the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 the Minister may make recommendations for wage adjustment` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Minister may make recommendations for wage adjustment"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 49 (src:2308-2312)
GIVEN `the recommendations have been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 the employer and the employer's employees or a trade union may negotiate based on the recommendations` MEANS
    IF `the recommendations have been published in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon the publication of the recommendations in the Gazette" -- "upon" counts as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05 (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 50 Interpretation for purposes of sections 48 and 49`

-- src:2319 | 50.—(1) Where a notice is served under section 18 of the Industrial
-- src:2320 | Relations Act 1960 by an employer or a trade union representing the
-- src:2321 | employer’s employees in respect of any matter referred to in
-- src:2322 | sections 48 and 49 and no agreement is reached between the
-- src:2323 | parties, either party may, despite the provisions of the Industrial
-- src:2324 | Relations Act 1960, refer the matter to the Industrial Arbitration
-- src:2325 | Court established under the Industrial Relations Act 1960 for
-- src:2326 | arbitration.
@ref s 50(1) (src:2319-2326)
GIVEN `a notice is served under section 18 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 by an employer or a trade union representing the employer's employees in respect of a matter referred to in sections 48 and 49` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no agreement is reached between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1) either party may refer the matter to the Industrial Arbitration Court for arbitration` MEANS
    IF `a notice is served under section 18 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 by an employer or a trade union representing the employer's employees in respect of a matter referred to in sections 48 and 49` AND `no agreement is reached between the parties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a notice is served under section 18 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 ... and no agreement is reached between the parties" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "Where" not met
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2330 | “annual wage supplement” means a single annual payment to
-- src:2331 | employees that is supplemental to the total amount of annual
-- src:2332 | wages earned by them, whether expressed as a percentage
-- src:2333 | thereof or otherwise;
@ref s 50(2) "annual wage supplement" (src:2330-2333)
GIVEN `the payment is a single annual payment to employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is supplemental to the total amount of annual wages earned by them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) "annual wage supplement" the payment is one` MEANS
    `the payment is a single annual payment to employees` AND `the payment is supplemental to the total amount of annual wages earned by them`

-- src:2335 | “variable payment” means such payment, however expressed
-- src:2336 | and whether paid annually or otherwise, which serves as an
-- src:2337 | incentive to all employees to increase their productivity or as
-- src:2338 | a reward for their contribution;
@ref s 50(2) "variable payment" (src:2335-2338)
GIVEN `the payment serves as an incentive to all employees to increase their productivity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment serves as a reward for their contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) "variable payment" the payment is one` MEANS
    `the payment serves as an incentive to all employees to increase their productivity` OR `the payment serves as a reward for their contribution`

-- src:2340 | “wages” means the basic wages payable to an employee in
-- src:2341 | respect of work done under his or her contract of service but
-- src:2342 | does not include any commission, overtime allowance or
-- src:2343 | other allowances payable to an employee.
@ref s 50(2) "wages" (src:2340-2343)
GIVEN `the payment is the basic wages payable to an employee in respect of work done under the employee's contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is a commission, an overtime allowance or another allowance payable to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) "wages" the payment is wages` MEANS
    `the payment is the basic wages payable to an employee in respect of work done under the employee's contract of service` AND (NOT `the payment is a commission, an overtime allowance or another allowance payable to the employee`)

§§ `s 52 Power to suspend application of this Part`

-- src:2349 | 52. The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, suspend the
-- src:2350 | application of any of the provisions of this Part to any classes of
-- src:2351 | employees when the public interest so requires it.
@ref s 52 (src:2349-2351)
GIVEN `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, suspended the application of the provision to a class of employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public interest so requires it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee belongs to that class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52 the provision of Part 4 is suspended for the employee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the public interest so requires it" -- "when" counts as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)): the public interest does not require it
        IF NOT `the public interest so requires it` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, suspended the application of the provision to a class of employees` AND `the employee belongs to that class` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, suspend the application of any of the provisions of this Part to any classes of employees" -- no notification has been made, or the employee is not in the class it names
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
§§ `s 53 Offence`

-- src:2355 | 53. Any employer who employs any person as an employee
-- src:2356 | contrary to the provisions of this Part or fails to pay any salary in
-- src:2357 | accordance with the provisions of this Part shall be guilty of an
-- src:2358 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2359 | $5,000, and for a second or subsequent offence to a fine not
-- src:2364 | exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:2365 | 12 months or to both.
@ref s 53 (src:2355-2365)
GIVEN `the employer employs a person as an employee contrary to the provisions of Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer fails to pay a salary in accordance with the provisions of Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53 the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer employs a person as an employee contrary to the provisions of Part 4` OR `the employer fails to pay a salary in accordance with the provisions of Part 4`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any employer who employs any person as an employee contrary to the provisions of this Part or fails to pay any salary in accordance with the provisions of this Part"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 53 (src:2355-2365)
GIVEN `the employer is guilty of an offence under section 53` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
`s 53 the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction"
        IF NOT `the employer is guilty of an offence under section 53` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the offence is a second or subsequent offence` THEN JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 10000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING)
